<title>UK: BAT gains amid renewed merger talk.</title>
<headline>BAT gains amid renewed merger talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BAT Industries Plc were indicated higher on Monday after the Sunday Telegraph said BAT was seeking a new merger partner after talks with Commercial Union broke down.</p>
<p>The shares were up 5p at 456-1/2p by 0816 GMT, in pre-market trade.</p>
<p>The newspaper said BAT still hopes to split its tobacco and financial services division and is keen to merge the latter with a major financial operator.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm sure BAT will continue to talk,&quot; said one trader. &quot;And if they put a deal together the shares are a pound too low.  </p>
<p>The group was initially rumoured to be in talks with Commercial Union over a 12.5 billion stg merger deal but the talks were said to have collapsed recently.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
